+++
title = "Creating Pages"
template = "docs"
+++

Revela provides commands to quickly create new pages. You can create:

<div class="features-grid">

### 📷 Gallery Pages

Photo collections with optional introductory text and sorting options.

### 📝 Text Pages

Content pages without image gallery (About, Contact, Imprint).

### 📊 Statistics Pages

EXIF analysis showing camera and lens usage statistics.

</div>

---

## Available Page Types

| Type | Description | Template |
|------|-------------|----------|
| `gallery` | Photo gallery with image grid | Default (body/gallery) |
| `text` | Text-only page without images | page |
| `statistics` | EXIF statistics | statistics/overview |
| `calendar` | Availability calendar | calendar/page |

> `statistics` and `calendar` are **plugin-provided** page types. In the Standalone edition they are always available. In the Full edition they appear once the Statistics or Calendar plugin is installed (`revela plugin install Statistics`, `revela plugin install Calendar`).

---

## Gallery Pages

Create a new gallery for your photos:

```bash
# Simple gallery
revela create page gallery vacation --title "Summer Vacation 2024"

# With description and sorting
revela create page gallery best-shots --title "Highlights" \
    --description "My best shots" \
    --sort "exif.raw.Rating:desc"

# Hidden gallery (not in navigation)
revela create page gallery drafts --title "Drafts" --hidden

# With a custom URL segment
revela create page gallery 2024-12-christmas --title "Christmas" --slug "xmas"
```

### Options

| Option | Alias | Description | Default |
|--------|-------|-------------|---------|
| `--title` | `-t` | Page title | "Gallery" |
| `--description` | `-d` | Description (for SEO) | "" |
| `--sort` | `-s` | Override sorting | (global) |
| `--hidden` | - | Hide from navigation | false |
| `--slug` | - | Custom URL segment | (folder name) |

### Sort Options

```bash
--sort "dateTaken:asc"        # Oldest first
--sort "dateTaken:desc"       # Newest first
--sort "filename:asc"         # A → Z
--sort "exif.raw.Rating:desc" # Highest rating first
--sort "exif.focalLength:asc" # Wide angle → telephoto
```

### Generated File

```toml
+++
title = "Summer Vacation 2024"
description = ""
+++
Add an optional introduction here.

This text appears above the image gallery.
```

### Text Around the Photos

To put text after the photos as well, place `[[gallery]]` on its own line where the
grid should appear:

```toml
+++
title = "Summer Vacation 2024"
+++
Two weeks on the coast.

[[gallery]]

More stories from the trip are in the other galleries.
```

`[[gallery: <filter>]]` shows a different selection at that spot, using the
[filter syntax](../filtering/), for example `[[gallery: all | sort random | limit 6]]`.

### Photos in Your Text

To show one of your photos in the text, put `[[photo: …]]` on its own line:

```markdown
The fence on the way to the lake:

[[photo: Years/2018/002190.jpg]]

We walked on for another hour.
```

The photo fills the width of the text and opens its photo page, like a photo in a
gallery. The × on the photo page brings visitors back to this page, right at the
photo. The photo page is created even when the page uses the lightbox or the photo
lives only in `_images/`.

To send visitors on to the photo's own gallery instead (the × then returns to that
gallery, for example 2018), add `| gallery`:

```markdown
[[photo: Years/2018/002190.jpg | gallery]]
```

Revela looks for the file in the page's folder, then in `_images/`, then as a path
from the source folder. Spaces in the path are fine as they are. If no photo matches,
`revela generate` shows a warning with the file and line, and the page shows nothing
at that spot. The photo's title (or its description) becomes the text for screen
readers.

For illustrations and screenshots that need no photo page, use a Markdown image. It
becomes the same responsive picture, without a link; put paths with spaces in `< >`:

```markdown
![The settings dialog](<_images/screenshots/settings dialog.png>)
```

### Open the Menu from Your Text

Lumina's menu opens without JavaScript, so a sentence can open it too. Write the
words as a button that targets the menu; Lumina styles it like a link:

```html
Browse the <button type="button" popovertarget="site-menu">photos of past years</button>.
```

All current browsers support this (Chrome and Edge 114, Safari 17, Firefox 125). In
older browsers the words still look like a link, but nothing happens.

---

## Text Pages

Create pages without image gallery (About, Contact, Imprint):

```bash
# About page
revela create page text about --title "About Me" \
    --description "Learn more about me and my photography"

# Contact page
revela create page text contact --title "Contact"

# Imprint (hidden from navigation)
revela create page text imprint --title "Imprint" --hidden
```

### Generated File

```toml
+++
title = "About Me"
description = "Learn more about me and my photography"
template = "page"
+++
Write your content here using **Markdown**.

## Example Heading

- List item one
- List item two
```

---

## Statistics Pages

Create a page with EXIF statistics of your photo collection:

```bash
revela create page statistics stats --title "Photo Statistics" \
    --description "Analysis of my camera and lens usage"
```

> **Note:** Statistics pages need the Statistics plugin and the Lumina.Statistics theme extension. Both are built into the Standalone edition. In the Full edition, install them with `revela plugin install Statistics` and `revela theme install Lumina.Statistics`. See [Statistics](../../plugins/statistics/).

### Generated File

```toml
+++
title = "Photo Statistics"
description = "EXIF statistics from your photo library"
template = "statistics/overview"
+++
```

---

## Calendar Pages

Show an availability calendar (booked and free days) from an iCal `.ics` file:

```bash
revela create page calendar availability --title "Availability" \
    --source bookings.ics --months 12
```

`--source` (required) is the `.ics` file, relative to the page folder. Put the file there yourself, or let the [Calendar Feeds](../../plugins/source-calendar/) plugin download it.

### Front Matter

```toml
+++
title = "Availability"
template = "calendar/page"
calendar.source = "bookings.ics"
calendar.months = 12
+++
```

See [Availability Calendar](../../plugins/calendar/) for modes, labels and languages.

---

## Interactive Mode

All page types support an interactive mode. Start without the path argument:

```bash
revela create page gallery
revela create page text
revela create page statistics
revela create page calendar
```

The wizard guides you through all options:

1. **Enter path** - Relative path to `source/`
2. **Title** - Enter page title
3. **Description** - Optional description
4. **Sorting** (gallery only) - Choose from presets or enter a custom field
5. **Hidden** - Hide from navigation?
6. **Slug** (gallery/text) - Custom URL segment
7. **Preview** - Show the generated front matter
8. **Confirm** - Create file?

> The wizard prompts follow each page type's own fields, so a text page skips the sorting step and a statistics page only asks for title and description.

---

## Frontmatter Fields

### All Page Types

| Field | Description |
|-------|-------------|
| `title` | Page title (in navigation and `<title>`) |
| `description` | SEO description |
| `hidden` | `true` = not in navigation (but accessible via URL) |
| `slug` | Overrides URL segment (last segment only) |
| `template` | Body template (default: `gallery` or `page`) |
| `cover` | Cover image path (relative to gallery or `_images/`) |

### Gallery Pages Only

| Field | Description |
|-------|-------------|
| `sort` | Override image sorting (e.g., `dateTaken:asc`) |
| `filter` | Filter expression to select images |

---

## Cover Images

Any page can display a cover/hero image:

```toml
+++
title = "My Gallery"
cover = "panorama.jpg"
+++
```

The cover uses the same path resolution as content images:
- `cover = "hero.jpg"`: image in the same folder
- `cover = "headers/banner.jpg"`: from the `_images/` folder
- `cover = "_images/banners/main.jpg"`: explicit `_images/` path

In templates, the cover is available as `{{ gallery.cover_image }}`, a full Image object
with `url`, `width`, `height`, `sizes`. Returns `null` when not set.

---

## Folder Structure

Pages are always created in the `source/` directory:

```
source/
├── vacation/
│   └── _index.revela      ← revela create page gallery vacation
├── about/
│   └── _index.revela      ← revela create page text about
└── stats/
    └── _index.revela      ← revela create page statistics stats
```

Nested paths are supported:

```bash
revela create page gallery "2024/summer/italy" --title "Italy 2024"
# Creates: source/2024/summer/italy/_index.revela
```

---

## Navigation Order

The order in navigation is determined by folder names:

```
source/
├── 01 Galleries/
│   ├── 01 Landscape/
│   └── 02 Portrait/
├── 02 About/
└── 03 Contact/
```

Use number prefixes for desired sorting. Numbers are stripped from the display title.

---

## Troubleshooting

If a page doesn't show up or the build fails, run `revela check`. It reports invalid front matter (with file and line), gallery folders that would end up at the same URL, and missing calendar files, each with a suggested fix.

